    <!-- ========================================================
         END BEHAVIOR (LEADING COEFFICIENT TEST) – PAGE 5
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="end-behavior">
        <title>End Behavior</title>

        <p>
            Whether the graph of a polynomial function eventually rises or falls (as <m>x \to -\infty</m> and <m>x \to \infty</m>) can be determined by the function's degree (even or odd) and by its leading coefficient, as indicated in the <term>Leading Coefficient Test</term>.
        </p>

        <p>
            <em>Notice that there are only 4 possibilities!</em>
        </p>

        <figure>
            <caption>Leading Coefficient Test</caption>
           <image source="images/evenodd.png" width="100%"/>
        </figure>
    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         END BEHAVIOR EXAMPLES (PAGE 6-8)
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="end-behavior-examples">
        <title>End Behavior Examples</title>

        <activity>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Describe the right-hand and left-hand behavior of the graph of each function.
                </p>
                <sidebyside widths="50% 50%">
                    <p><strong>a.</strong> <m>f(x) = -x^3 + 4x</m></p>
                    <p><strong>b.</strong> <m>g(x) = x^4 - 5x^2 + 4</m></p>
                </sidebyside>
                <sidebyside widths="50% 50%">
                    <p><strong>c.</strong> <m>h(x) = x^5 - x</m></p>
                    <p><strong>d.</strong> <m>k(x) = -2(x - 5)(x + 1)^3</m></p>
                </sidebyside>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p><em>a.</em> <m>f(x) = -x^3 + 4x</m> has degree 3 (odd) and leading coefficient -1 (negative). So the graph falls to the right and rises to the left.</p>
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>f(x) = -x^3 + 4x</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}
                            \begin{axis}[
                                width=7.0cm,
                                height=5.0cm,
                                xmin=-7, xmax=7,
                                ymin=-5, ymax=5,
                                axis lines=middle,
                                grid=both,
                                grid style={gray!18},
                                axis line style={gray!60},
                                xlabel={$x$},
                                ylabel={$y$},
                                xtick={-6,-5,...,6},
                                ytick={-5,-4,...,5},
                                clip=false
                            ]
                            \addplot[blue!75!black, thick, domain=-2.5:2.5, samples=300] {-x^3+4*x};
                            \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (axis cs:2.0,2.0) {$f(x)=-x^3+4x$};
                            \end{axis}
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>

                <p><em>b.</em> <m>g(x) = x^4 - 5x^2 + 4</m> has degree 4 (even) and leading coefficient 1 (positive). So the graph rises to the right and rises to the left.</p>
                <!-- Corrected graph for g(x) -->
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>g(x) = x^4 - 5x^2 + 4</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}
                            \begin{axis}[
                                width=7.0cm,
                                height=5.0cm,
                                xmin=-4, xmax=4,
                                ymin=-4, ymax=6,
                                axis lines=middle,
                                grid=both,
                                grid style={gray!18},
                                axis line style={gray!60},
                                xlabel={$x$},
                                ylabel={$y$},
                                xtick={-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4},
                                ytick={-4,-2,0,2,4,6},
                                clip=true
                            ]
                            \addplot[blue!75!black, thick, domain=-2.5:2.5, samples=300] {x^4-5*x^2+4};
                            \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (axis cs:2.0,4.5) {$g(x)=x^4-5x^2+4$};
                            \end{axis}
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>

                <p><em>c.</em> <m>h(x) = x^5 - x</m> has degree 5 (odd) and leading coefficient 1 (positive). So the graph rises to the right and falls to the left.</p>
                <!-- Corrected graph for h(x) -->
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>h(x) = x^5 - x</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.36cm,y=0.36cm,>=stealth,line cap=round,line join=round]
                                \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-12,-6) grid (12,12);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thin, ->] (-12,0) -- (12.35,0);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thin, ->] (0,-6) -- (0,12.35);
                                \foreach \x in {-12,-11,...,11} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (\x,-0.16) -- (\x,0.16);
                                \foreach \y in {-6,-5,...,11} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (-0.16,\y) -- (0.16,\y);
                                \foreach \x in {-12,-10,-8,-6,-4,-2,2,4,6,8,10,12} \node[gray!55!black,font=\scriptsize,anchor=north] at (\x,-0.20) {\x};
                                \foreach \y in {-6,-4,-2,2,4,6,8,10,12} \node[gray!55!black,font=\scriptsize,anchor=east] at (-0.20,\y) {\y};
                                \clip (-12,-6) rectangle (12,12);
                                \draw[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-2:2, samples=300] plot (\x,{\x^5-\x});
                                \node[blue!75!black, font=\large, anchor=west] at (2.2,2.0) {$h(x)=x^5-x$};
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>

                <p><em>d.</em> <m>k(x) = -2(x - 5)(x + 1)^3</m> has degree 1+3=4 (even) and leading coefficient -2 (negative). So the graph falls to the right and falls to the left.</p>
                <!-- Corrected graph for k(x) -->
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>k(x) = -2(x-5)(x+1)^3</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.36cm,y=0.0144cm,>=stealth,line cap=round,line join=round]
                                \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-14,-300) grid[step=1] (19,300);
                                \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-14,-300) grid[step=50] (19,300);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thin, ->] (-14,0) -- (19.5,0);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thin, ->] (0,-310) -- (0,310);
                                \foreach \x in {-14,-13,...,19} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (\x,-0.5) -- (\x,0.5);
                                \foreach \y in {-300,-250,-200,-150,-100,-50,50,100,150,200,250,300}
                                    \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (-0.5,\y) -- (0.5,\y);
                                \foreach \x in {-14,-12,-10,-8,-6,-4,-2,2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,18}
                                    \node[gray!55!black,font=\tiny,anchor=north] at (\x,-0.3) {\x};
                                \foreach \y in {-300,-250,-200,-150,-100,-50,50,100,150,200,250,300}
                                    \node[gray!55!black,font=\tiny,anchor=east] at (-0.3,\y) {\y};
                                \clip (-14,-300) rectangle (19,300);
                                \draw[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-4.5:7.5, samples=400] plot (\x,{-2*(\x-5)*(\x+1)^3});
                                \node[blue!75!black, font=\large, anchor=west] at (5.5,250) {$k(x)=-2(x-5)(x+1)^3$};
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>
            </solution>
        </activity>
    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         ZEROS OF POLYNOMIAL FUNCTIONS (PAGE 9-10)
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="zeros-of-polynomials">
        <title>Zeros of Polynomial Functions</title>

        <definition>
            <title>Zeros of a Polynomial</title>
            <p>
                The values of <m>x</m> in the domain of <m>f</m> for which <m>f(x) = 0</m> are called the <term>zeros</term> of the function. These are the real solutions (or roots) of the equation <m>f(x) = 0</m> and correspond to the <m>x</m>-intercepts of the graph of <m>y = f(x)</m>.
            </p>
        </definition>

        <p>
            <em>Related statements:</em>
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><m>c</m> is a zero of the function</li>
            <li><m>c</m> is a solution (or root) of the equation <m>f(x)=0</m></li>
            <li><m>c</m> is an <m>x</m>-intercept of the graph of <m>f</m></li>
            <li><m>(x - c)</m> is a factor of <m>f(x)</m></li>
        </ul>

        <activity>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the zeros of <m>f(x) = x^3 - 5x^2 - 4x + 20</m> by factoring.
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    Factor by grouping:
                </p>
                <me>f(x) = x^2(x - 5) - 4(x - 5) = (x^2 - 4)(x - 5) = (x - 2)(x + 2)(x - 5)</me>
                <p>
                    Zeros: <m>x = 2</m>, <m>x = -2</m>, <m>x = 5</m>.
                </p>

                <!-- Corrected graph for f(x) = x^3 - 5x^2 - 4x + 20 -->
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>f(x) = x^3 - 5x^2 - 4x + 20</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}
                            \begin{axis}[
                                width=8.0cm,
                                height=6.0cm,
                                xmin=-4.5, xmax=7.5,
                                ymin=-16, ymax=26,
                                axis lines=middle,
                                axis line style={gray!70!black},
                                grid=both,
                                grid style={gray!25, dashed},
                                major grid style={gray!35, dashed},
                                xlabel={$x$},
                                ylabel={$y$},
                                xtick={-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7},
                                ytick={-15,-10,-5,5,10,15,20,25},
                                clip=true
                            ]
                            \addplot[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-3.5:6.5, samples=400] {x^3 - 5*x^2 - 4*x + 20};
                            \addplot[only marks, mark=*, mark size=3pt, red] coordinates {(-2,0) (2,0) (5,0)};
                            \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=south west] at (axis cs:0.5,-17) {$f(x)=x^3-5x^2-4x+20$};
                            \end{axis}
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>
            </solution>
        </activity>
    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         MULTIPLICITY AND TOUCH/CROSS (PAGE 11)
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="multiplicity">
        <title>Multiplicity and Touch/Cross</title>

        <definition>
            <title>Multiplicity</title>
            <p>
                If a polynomial function has a factor <m>(x - c)</m> that appears exactly <m>n</m> times, then <m>c</m> is a zero of <term>multiplicity</term> <m>n</m>.
                In other words, if the factor <m>(x-c)^n </m> is a factor of the polynomial, <m>c</m> is a zero of multiplicity of <m>n</m>. 
            </p>
            <p>
                If <m>c</m> is a zero of <em>odd</em> multiplicity, then the graph <em effect="bold">crosses</em> the <m>x</m>-axis at <m>c</m>.
            </p>
            <p>
                If <m>c</m> is a zero of <em>even</em> multiplicity, then the graph <em effect="bold">touches</em> the <m>x</m>-axis at <m>c</m> (bounces off).
            </p>
        </definition>
<p>
    Compare the following functions.  How does the exponent on the <m>(x-3)</m> factor affect the <m>x</m>-intercept? 
</p>
        <sidebyside widths="33% 33% 33%">
            <figure>
                <caption><m>x=3</m> cross (odd multiplicity)</caption>
                <image width="100%">
                    <latex-image>
                        <![CDATA[
                        \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                        \begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
    width=6.0cm,
    height=4.8cm,
    xmin=-3.8, xmax=4.5,
    ymin=-10, ymax=6,
    axis lines=middle,
    grid=both,
    grid style={gray!18},
    axis line style={gray!60},
    xlabel={$x$},
    ylabel={$y$},
    xtick={-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4},
    ytick={-8,-6,-4,-2,2,4,6},
    clip=true % <-- FIXED: clips the plot to the axis box
]
\addplot[blue!75!black, thick, domain=-3.2:4.0, samples=300] {x*(x+2)*(x-3)};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*, mark size=3pt, red] coordinates {(-2,0) (0,0) (3,0)};
\node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (axis cs:-2,-9) {$f(x)=x(x+2)(x-3)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

                        \end{adjustbox}
                        ]]>
                    </latex-image>
                </image>
            </figure>

            <!-- Corrected graph for f(x) = x(x+2)(x-3)^2 -->
            <figure>
                <caption><m>x=3</m> touches (even multiplicity)</caption>
                <image width="100%">
                    <latex-image>
                        <![CDATA[
                        \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                        \begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.18cm,>=stealth,line cap=round,line join=round]
                            \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-4,-18) grid[step=1] (5,15);
                            \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-4,-18) grid[step=3] (5,15);
                            \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (-4.2,0) -- (5.2,0);
                            \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (0,-18.2) -- (0,15.2);
                            \foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (\x,-0.15) -- (\x,0.15);
                            \foreach \y in {-18,-15,-12,-9,-6,-3,3,6,9,12,15} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (-0.15,\y) -- (0.15,\y);
                            \foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=north] at (\x,-0.25) {\x};
                            \foreach \y in {-18,-15,-12,-9,-6,-3,3,6,9,12,15} \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=east] at (-0.25,\y) {\y};
                            \clip (-4,-18) rectangle (7,15);
                            \draw[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-3.8:4.8, samples=500] plot (\x,{(\x)*(\x+2)*(\x-3)^2});
                            \draw[red, fill=red] (-2,0) circle (3pt);
                            \draw[red, fill=red] (0,0) circle (3pt);
                            \draw[red, fill=red] (3,0) circle (3pt);
                            \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (-0.5,-9) {$f(x)=x(x+2)(x-3)^2$};
                        \end{tikzpicture}
                        \end{adjustbox}
                        ]]>
                    </latex-image>
                </image>
            </figure>

            <!-- Corrected graph for f(x) = x(x+2)(x-3)^3 -->
            <figure>
                <caption><m>x=3</m> crosses (odd multiplicity)</caption>
                <image width="100%">
                    <latex-image>
                        <![CDATA[
                        \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                        \begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.055cm,>=stealth,line cap=round,line join=round]
                            \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-3,-30) grid[step=1] (5,80);
                            \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-3,-30) grid[step=10] (5,80);
                            \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (-3.2,0) -- (5.2,0);
                            \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (0,-32) -- (0,82);
                            \foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (\x,-0.15) -- (\x,0.15);
                            \foreach \y in {-30,-20,-10,10,20,30,40,50,60,70,80} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (-0.15,\y) -- (0.15,\y);
                            \foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=north] at (\x,-0.25) {\x};
                            \foreach \y in {-30,-20,-10,10,20,30,40,50,60,70,80} \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=east] at (-0.25,\y) {\y};
                            \clip (-3,-30) rectangle (5,80);
                            \draw[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-2.8:4.5, samples=500] plot (\x,{(\x)*(\x+2)*(\x-3)^3});
                            \draw[red, fill=red] (-2,0) circle (3pt);
                            \draw[red, fill=red] (0,0) circle (3pt);
                            \draw[red, fill=red] (3,0) circle (3pt);
                            \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (-2.8,75) {$f(x)=x(x+2)(x-3)^3$};
                        \end{tikzpicture}
                        \end{adjustbox}
                        ]]>
                    </latex-image>
                </image>
            </figure>
        </sidebyside>
    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         YOU TRY: EXAMPLE – PAGE 12-13
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="example-graph-polynomial-1">
        <title>You Try:</title>

        <activity>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Given <m>f(x) = 3x^3 - 6x^2 + 3x</m>, find all real zeros, determine their multiplicity, then graph the function.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <em>Steps:</em>
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Factored form</li>
                    <li>End Behavior</li>
                    <li>Intercepts (y-intercept and x-intercepts with multiplicities)</li>
                    <li>Check points</li>
                </ul>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <em>Factored form:</em>
                </p>
                <me>f(x) = 3x(x^2 - 2x + 1) = 3x(x - 1)^2</me>

                <p>
                    <em>End Behavior:</em> Degree 3 (odd), leading coefficient 3 (positive) → falls to the left, rises to the right.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <em>Intercepts:</em>
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>y-intercept: <m>f(0) = 0</m></li>
                    <li>x-intercepts: <m>x = 0</m> (multiplicity 1, odd → crosses), <m>x = 1</m> (multiplicity 2, even → touches)</li>
                </ul>

                <p>
                    <em>Check points:</em> e.g., <m>f(-1) = -12</m>, <m>f(2) = 6</m>.
                </p>

                <!-- Corrected graph for f(x) = 3x(x-1)^2 -->
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>f(x) = 3x(x-1)^2</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.6cm,>=stealth,line cap=round,line join=round]
                                \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-4,-4) grid[step=1] (4,4);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (-4.2,0) -- (4.2,0);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (0,-4.2) -- (0,4.2);
                                \foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (\x,-0.15) -- (\x,0.15);
                                \foreach \y in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (-0.15,\y) -- (0.15,\y);
                                \foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=north] at (\x,-0.25) {\x};
                                \foreach \y in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=east] at (-0.25,\y) {\y};
                                \clip (-4,-4) rectangle (4,4);
                                \draw[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-0.8:2.3, samples=400] plot (\x,{3*(\x)*(\x-1)^2});
                                \draw[red, fill=red] (0,0) circle (3pt);
                                \draw[red, fill=red] (1,0) circle (3pt);
                                \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (-4,3.5) {$f(x)=3x(x-1)^2$};
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>
            </solution>
        </activity>
    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         ANOTHER EXAMPLE – PAGE 15-17
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="example-graph-polynomial-2">
        

        <activity>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Given <m>f(x) = 2x^4 + 2x^2 - 40</m>, find all real zeros, determine their multiplicity, then graph the function.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <em>Steps:</em>
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Factored form</li>
                    <li>End Behavior</li>
                    <li>Intercepts (y-intercept and x-intercepts with multiplicities)</li>
                    <li>Check points</li>
                </ul>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <em>Factored form:</em>
                </p>
                <me>f(x) = 2(x^4 + x^2 - 20) = 2(x^2 + 5)(x^2 - 4) = 2(x^2 + 5)(x - 2)(x + 2)</me>

                <p>
                    <em>End Behavior:</em> Degree 4 (even), leading coefficient 2 (positive) → rises to the right and left.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <em>Intercepts:</em>
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>y-intercept: <m>f(0) = -40</m></li>
                    <li>x-intercepts: <m>x = -2</m> (multiplicity 1, odd → crosses), <m>x = 2</m> (multiplicity 1, odd → crosses).</li>
                    <li>The factor <m>(x^2 + 5)</m> has no real zeros.</li>
                </ul>

                <!-- Corrected graph for f(x) = 2(x^2+5)(x-2)(x+2) -->
                <figure>
                    <caption>Graph of <m>f(x) = 2(x^2+5)(x-2)(x+2)</m></caption>
                    <image width="60%">
                        <latex-image>
                            <![CDATA[
                            \begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}
                            \begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.06cm,>=stealth,line cap=round,line join=round]
                                \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-5,-45) grid[step=1] (4,40);
                                \draw[gray!25, very thin] (-5,-45) grid[step=5] (4,40);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (-5.2,0) -- (4.2,0);
                                \draw[gray!55!black, thick, ->] (0,-46) -- (0,41);
                                \foreach \x in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (\x,-0.15) -- (\x,0.15);
                                \foreach \y in {-45,-40,-35,-30,-25,-20,-15,-10,-5,5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40}
                                    \draw[gray!50!black, very thin] (-0.15,\y) -- (0.15,\y);
                                \foreach \x in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4}
                                    \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=north] at (\x,-0.25) {\x};
                                \foreach \y in {-40,-30,-20,-10,10,20,30,40}
                                    \node[gray!55!black,font=\small,anchor=east] at (-0.25,\y) {\y};
                                \clip (-5,-50) rectangle (4,40);
                                \draw[blue!75!black, very thick, domain=-3.5:3.5, samples=500] plot (\x,{2*(\x)^4+2*(\x)^2-40});
                                \draw[red, fill=red] (-2,0) circle (3pt);
                                \draw[red, fill=red] (2,0) circle (3pt);
                                \node[blue!75!black, font=\small, anchor=west] at (-4.5,-46) {$f(x)=2(x^2+5)(x-2)(x+2)$};
                            \end{tikzpicture}
                            \end{adjustbox}
                            ]]>
                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>
            </solution>
        </activity>
    </subsection>

</section>